/T (Extend the contextual RL framework to railway reservation by treating seat allocation as a contextual bandit problem. Incorporate passenger demand forecasting, waitlist prediction, cancellation probabilities, and real-time booking behavior to recommend optimal seat allocation while minimizing waiting time and maximizing occupancy.  Extend the hierarchical DRL framework to railway reservation by treating seat  allocation as a sequential decision-making problem. Integrate passenger deman forecasting, cancellation prediction, waitlist prioritization, coach occupancy  balancing, and dynamic reservation policies to maximize seat utilization while  reducing waiting-list length and improving passenger satisfaction.  Develop an LLM-powered Smart Railway Reservation System by combining LLM reasoning with demand forecasting, passenger preference analysis, reinforcement learning for dynamic seat allocation, RAG for railway policy retrieval, and predictive models for cancellations and waitlist confirmation. This would optimize seat utilization, reduce waitlist length, improve passenger satisfaction, and support real-time reservation decision-making.  Extend the LHC-DQN framework to railway reservation systems by integrating  passenger demand forecasting, cancellation prediction, dynamic seat allocation RAC/waitlist prioritization, and real-time reservation queue optimization. )
/E (Extend the contextual RL framework to railway reservation by treating seat allocation as a contextual bandit problem. Incorporate passenger demand forecasting, waitlist prediction, cancellation probabilities, and real-time booking behavior to recommend optimal seat allocation while minimizing waiting time and maximizing occupancy.  Extend the hierarchical DRL framework to railway reservation by treating seat  allocation as a sequential decision-making problem. Integrate passenger deman forecasting, cancellation prediction, waitlist prioritization, coach occupancy  balancing, and dynamic reservation policies to maximize seat utilization while  reducing waiting-list length and improving passenger satisfaction.  Develop an LLM-powered Smart Railway Reservation System by combining LLM reasoning with demand forecasting, passenger preference analysis, reinforcement learning for dynamic seat allocation, RAG for railway policy retrieval, and predictive models for cancellations and waitlist confirmation. This would optimize seat utilization, reduce waitlist length, improve passenger satisfaction, and support real-time reservation decision-making.  Extend the LHC-DQN framework to railway reservation systems by integrating  passenger demand forecasting, cancellation prediction, dynamic seat allocation RAC/waitlist prioritization, and real-time reservation queue optimization. )
